+/*
+ * iPod touch 5G (N78AP, S5L8942X "A5", -M iPod-Touch-5G) and iPhone 5 (N41AP, S5L8950X "A6", -M iPhone-5).
+ *
+ * The A6's arm-io map is the A5's block for block (ClassicTouch docs/reports/a6-step1.md 2), so the iPhone 5
+ * is this machine with another N78Board: Swift cores, 1 GiB, a third I2C bus, other GPIOs.
+ *
+ * Step 1 of the A5 track (ClassicTouch docs/research/ios8-10-step0.md §7):
+ * enter the 7.1.2 (11D257) and 9.3.5 (13G36) kernels from a kboot bundle and
+ * get their console on uart1, up to "Waiting for root device". One Cortex-A9
+ * (the DT's cpu1 is hidden by kboot), 512 MiB of DRAM at 0x80000000, the AIC
+ * in place of the A4's PL192s. Everything else in the arm-io window logs as
+ * an unimplemented device (-d unimp) until bring-up shows what the kernel
+ * needs next.
+ *
+ * Boot input is the A4 machine's kboot bundle (hw/arm/ipad1.c): a flat image
+ * of physical memory, optional K48SEG segments, and the 24-byte K48KBOOT
+ * trailer {magic[8]; u32 load_pa, entry_pa, bootargs_pa, image_len}. The CPU
+ * starts at entry_pa in SVC mode with the MMU off and r0 = bootargs_pa.
+ */
